From: Michael Narine <michael@verita-ai.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] deps: build zlib 1.2.13 against the macOS 15 SDK (fdopen macro)

zutil.h defines fdopen(fd,mode) as NULL when TARGET_OS_MAC is set. The macOS 15
SDK (Xcode 16, the macos-15 runner image) declares fdopen() in <stdio.h> with
availability attributes after that macro has expanded, so zutil.c fails with
"error: expected identifier or '('". macOS has a real fdopen(), so pass
-Dfdopen=fdopen on Apple to make the macro a no-op. The C flags passed to the
zlib project replace the ones from DEP_CMAKE_OPTS, so the availability checks
are repeated.

Purpose: Let the zlib dependency compile with the macOS 15 SDK.
SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
Upstream-Status: Pending
Orca-Base: v2.4.2
---
diff --git a/deps/ZLIB/ZLIB.cmake b/deps/ZLIB/ZLIB.cmake
index 0d5497e4..c08ada59 100644
--- a/deps/ZLIB/ZLIB.cmake
+++ b/deps/ZLIB/ZLIB.cmake
@@ -1,5 +1,14 @@
 set(patch_command git init && ${PATCH_CMD} ${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/0001-Respect-BUILD_SHARED_LIBS.patch)
 
+set(_zlib_osx_args "")
+if (APPLE)
+  # zutil.h (up to and including 1.2.13) defines fdopen(fd,mode) as NULL when TARGET_OS_MAC is set,
+  # which breaks the declaration in <stdio.h> of the macOS 15 SDK (Xcode 16). Macs have a real
+  # fdopen(), so make the macro a no-op. -DCMAKE_C_FLAGS here replaces the one from DEP_CMAKE_OPTS,
+  # so repeat the availability checks.
+  set(_zlib_osx_args "-DCMAKE_C_FLAGS=${DEP_WERRORS_SDK} -Dfdopen=fdopen")
+endif ()
+
 orcaslicer_add_cmake_project(ZLIB
   # GIT_REPOSITORY https://github.com/madler/zlib.git
   # GIT_TAG v1.2.11
@@ -11,5 +20,6 @@ orcaslicer_add_cmake_project(ZLIB
   CMAKE_ARGS
     -DSKIP_INSTALL_FILES=ON         # Prevent installation of man pages et al.
     -DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON
+    ${_zlib_osx_args}
 )
 
